/*
  NewVersionBanner.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0129 · NewVersionBanner (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The three keys at the top mirror the web
  source (components/feedback/NewVersionBanner.tsx) one-for-one — the availability message and the
  "Later" / "Reload" action labels (web `t('app.newVersion.message' | 'app.newVersion.later' |
  'app.newVersion.reload', …)`). The remaining keys are the native P4 leaf chrome (loading a11y, the
  up-to-date empty card, the boot-probe error tile, the freshness axis, and the VoiceOver version
  detail) so the Swift sources hold no English literals.

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are
  kept in a per-surface table ("NewVersionBanner") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings
  without editing the shared catalog. In test / preview bundles `NSLocalizedString` returns the value
  below, keeping the labels deterministic.
*/

/* --- Web source keys (NewVersionBanner.tsx) --- */
"app.newVersion.message" = "A new version of TeslaSync is available.";
"app.newVersion.later" = "Later";
"app.newVersion.reload" = "Reload";

/* --- Loading / empty / error chrome (P4 leaf contract) --- */
"app.newVersion.loadingA11y" = "Checking for updates";
"app.newVersion.upToDateTitle" = "You're on the latest version";
"app.newVersion.upToDateMessage" = "TeslaSync is up to date. A notice appears here when a new version is deployed.";
"app.newVersion.errorTitle" = "Couldn't check for updates";
"app.newVersion.retry" = "Retry";

/* --- VoiceOver version detail (accessible parity of the status row) --- */
"app.newVersion.versionDetailA11y" = "Version {version}";

/* --- Freshness (P4 connectivity axis) --- */
"app.newVersion.live" = "Live";
"app.newVersion.stale" = "Stale";
"app.newVersion.offline" = "Offline";
"app.newVersion.staleA11y" = "Update check is stale — tap to refresh";
"app.newVersion.offlineA11y" = "Offline — showing the last known version";
